# promise: web-extension-open-popup
# web-features: an extension opens its own popup (chrome.action.openPopup(): 1Password's inline menu, a
# shortcut's popup). Chrome opens it only in the active window, and asked the page's Browser window, which on
# the engine is never seen and never active: every call failed ("Could not find an active browser window",
# or for a given window "Cannot show popup for an inactive window"). cra-extension-popup-window.patch asks Cra
# whether the page's own window is the one in use, and the popup comes up in Cra's popup frame
# (ExtensionPopupWindow), as one from the extension's button does. Both forms: the current window and the
# page's window by id. It takes the screen: Cra has to be the app in use.
requires screen
env CRA_TEST_BACKGROUND=0
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true}
extension ${FIXTURES}/OpenPopupExtension
cra://debug?windowSize=1200x800
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=front
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
cra://debug?activate=1
wait 1
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=open-popup
expect-log GET /page\.html\?n=openpopup-open-popup-opened
expect-log extension popup shown
cra://dismiss
wait 1
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=open-popup-window
expect-log GET /page\.html\?n=openpopup-open-popup-window-opened
cra://dismiss
reject-log openpopup-[a-z-]*-error
reject-log fault:
